    "body": "> But since all browsers do the same thing that deviates from the spec, we should consider changing the spec to match browsers.\n\nRegardless of the specifics of the behavior being discussed, I will almost always agree with this sentence. Unless that behavior is really bad. In this case, it actually seems good - it allows some performance optimizations, for example, at least in Chromium. So I'm supportive of changing the spec to match behavior. I don't have opinions on the particular choice of how to do that.",
