    "updated_at": "2026-06-24T16:05:06Z",
    "body": "As noted in whatwg/dom#1474, I think the right approach here is to make it so that the fragment parser inserts directly to the fragment rather than to the inert document. This can be done by [adjusting the insertion location](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#appropriate-place-for-inserting-a-node) to the fragment when trying to insert to the inert document's root. \n\nIt would have the effect of elements not being connected during fragment parser, and would be a better match of how implementations do this. \n\nCoincidentally, a lot of work in this area is done for steaming parser/sanitizer and out of order HTML streaming, so I can probably add in a PR that fixes this problem in between or I can guide you on how to do that after. ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
